[skill_feature_hitpoints_overview_0]
columns=10
table=skill_features
columndef=0:icon,obj
values=0:0:744
columndef=2:text,string
values=2:0:Hitpoints are used to tell you how healthy your character is. A character who reaches 0 Hitpoints has died\\, but will reappear in their chosen respawn location (normally Lumbridge).
columndef=3:skill,int,int,int
values=3:0:6,-1,0
columndef=6:membersonly,boolean
values=6:0:0

[skill_feature_hitpoints_overview_1]
columns=10
table=skill_features
columndef=0:icon,obj
values=0:0:379
columndef=2:text,string
values=2:0:As with any skill\\, you will restore 1 missing Hitpoint every minute\\, but the best way of recovering Hitpoints is by eating food.
columndef=3:skill,int,int,int
values=3:0:6,-1,0
columndef=6:membersonly,boolean
values=6:0:0

[skill_feature_hitpoints_overview_2]
columns=10
table=skill_features
columndef=0:icon,obj
values=0:0:7620
columndef=2:text,string
values=2:0:If you see any red 'hit splats' during combat\\, the number shown corresponds to the number of Hitpoints lost as a result of that strike.
columndef=3:skill,int,int,int
values=3:0:6,-1,0
columndef=6:membersonly,boolean
values=6:0:0

[skill_feature_hitpoints_overview_3]
columns=10
table=skill_features
columndef=0:icon,obj
values=0:0:7620
columndef=2:text,string
values=2:0:Blue hit splats mean no damage has been dealt.
columndef=3:skill,int,int,int
values=3:0:6,-1,0
columndef=6:membersonly,boolean
values=6:0:0

[skill_feature_hitpoints_overview_4]
columns=10
