[skill_feature_magic_overview_0]
columns=10
table=skill_features
columndef=0:icon,obj
values=0:0:579
columndef=2:text,string
values=2:0:Magic grants you access to a wide variety of spells. To cast each spell\\, you will need a specific set of runes.<br>Select a spell in this guide to see what runes it requires.
columndef=3:skill,int,int,int
values=3:0:4,-1,0
columndef=6:membersonly,boolean
values=6:0:0

[skill_feature_magic_overview_1]
columns=10
table=skill_features
columndef=0:icon,obj
values=0:0:1017
columndef=2:text,string
values=2:0:Select a spell on the 'Magic' side-panel to begin casting it.<br>If a spell is supposed to work on a nearby monster\\, player or object\\, you should select the spell\\, then select the target on which you wish to cast the spell.
columndef=3:skill,int,int,int
values=3:0:4,-1,0
columndef=6:membersonly,boolean
values=6:0:0

[skill_feature_magic_overview_2]
columns=10
table=skill_features
columndef=0:icon,obj
values=0:0:1379
columndef=2:text,string
values=2:0:Staves can also be used to auto-cast certain offensive spells in combat. To enable this\\, equip your staff\\, go to the 'Combat Options' side panel\\, and select one of the 'Spell' options.
columndef=3:skill,int,int,int
values=3:0:4,-1,0
columndef=6:membersonly,boolean
values=6:0:0

[skill_feature_magic_overview_3]
columns=10
table=skill_features
columndef=0:icon,obj
values=0:0:1381
columndef=2:text,string
values=2:0:You can use certain pieces of equipment to replace runes in order to cast spells. For instance\\, an equipped Staff of Air counts as an infinite supply of air runes.
columndef=3:skill,int,int,int
values=3:0:4,-1,0
columndef=6:membersonly,boolean
values=6:0:0

