[skill_feature_mining_overview_0]
columns=10
table=skill_features
columndef=0:icon,obj
values=0:0:1267
columndef=2:text,string
values=2:0:Mining allows you to get various minerals from the world for use in other skills\\, primarily Smithing.
columndef=3:skill,int,int,int
values=3:0:13,-1,0
columndef=6:membersonly,boolean
values=6:0:0

[skill_feature_mining_overview_1]
columns=10
table=skill_features
columndef=0:icon,obj
values=0:0:440
columndef=2:text,string
values=2:0:To mine a rock\\, simply interact with it while holding a pickaxe you have the level to use and you'll start mining it. Eventually\\, you'll collect the ore and the rock will deplete. Low-level rocks will replenish themselves fairly quickly\\, but higher-level ones will take longer and longer to come back.
columndef=3:skill,int,int,int
values=3:0:13,-1,0
columndef=6:membersonly,boolean
values=6:0:0

[skill_feature_mining_overview_2]
columns=10
table=skill_features
columndef=0:icon,obj
values=0:0:1275
columndef=2:text,string
values=2:0:At higher Mining levels\\, you'll have an increased chance of successfully mining a rock. You'll also be able to use more powerful pickaxes\\, which decrease the amount of time between mining attempts.
columndef=3:skill,int,int,int
values=3:0:13,-1,0
columndef=6:membersonly,boolean
values=6:0:0

[skill_feature_mining_overview_3]
columns=10
table=skill_features
columndef=0:icon,obj
values=0:0:444
columndef=2:text,string
values=2:0:Note that while most pickaxes have an Attack level requirement to equip them\\, you're still able to use them from within your inventory if you have the required Mining level.
columndef=3:skill,int,int,int
values=3:0:13,-1,0
columndef=6:membersonly,boolean
values=6:0:0

